-- Catalog X-watch batch 2026-11-26 (Launchpad HQ)
-- Guarded SQL only. Platforms table. Idempotent. Update statements only.
-- No user tables. No new slugs.
-- UPDATE: windsurf (Devin Desktop / Cognition), aleph-alpha-luminous,
--          openai-api, manus
-- aleph-alpha-luminous.description was null on the 2026-11-26 read-only
-- check, so the first run sets the description to the note alone.
-- SKIP as rows: Sand AI MAGI-2 (no Sand or MAGI row; developer API, not a
--               new slug), Decart (no row; Amazon's 2026-11-23 post is an
--               agreement to buy the Optimization Stack technology and hire
--               the co-founders and team, still subject to closing conditions,
--               and it does not say a Decart product is discontinued).
-- Sources checked 2026-11-26 on vendor pages (see PR body). Not run from here.

UPDATE platforms SET description = CASE
  WHEN COALESCE(description, $xw$$xw$) = $xw$$xw$ THEN $xw$Note (2026-11-26): Cognition's post dated 2026-11-24 says SWE-2.1 is a coding model trained with pure reinforcement learning on Kimi K3, and that it is an upgrade over SWE-2. SWE-2.1 Ultrafast is that same model, served through a Cerebras partnership at 10 times the speed. The post does not list a price. The post also says SWE-2.1 Cyber, a version with more permissive safeguards, is rolling out to Devin Security.$xw$
  ELSE description || $xw$ Note (2026-11-26): Cognition's post dated 2026-11-24 says SWE-2.1 is a coding model trained with pure reinforcement learning on Kimi K3, and that it is an upgrade over SWE-2. SWE-2.1 Ultrafast is that same model, served through a Cerebras partnership at 10 times the speed. The post does not list a price. The post also says SWE-2.1 Cyber, a version with more permissive safeguards, is rolling out to Devin Security.$xw$
END, "updatedAt" = now() WHERE slug = $xw$windsurf$xw$ AND COALESCE(description, $xw$$xw$) NOT LIKE $xw$%SWE-2.1 Ultrafast is that same model%$xw$;

UPDATE platforms SET description = CASE
  WHEN COALESCE(description, $xw$$xw$) = $xw$$xw$ THEN $xw$Note (2026-11-26): Aleph Alpha's news post dated 23 November 2026 says Kolibri 1.1 is an open-weight language model, available on Hugging Face under the Apache 2.0 license. The post says it has 75 billion total parameters and 3 billion active parameters. Recorded on this row, not as a new row.$xw$
  ELSE description || $xw$ Note (2026-11-26): Aleph Alpha's news post dated 23 November 2026 says Kolibri 1.1 is an open-weight language model, available on Hugging Face under the Apache 2.0 license. The post says it has 75 billion total parameters and 3 billion active parameters. Recorded on this row, not as a new row.$xw$
END, "updatedAt" = now() WHERE slug = $xw$aleph-alpha-luminous$xw$ AND COALESCE(description, $xw$$xw$) NOT LIKE $xw$%Kolibri 1.1 is an open-weight language model%$xw$;

UPDATE platforms SET description = CASE
  WHEN COALESCE(description, $xw$$xw$) = $xw$$xw$ THEN $xw$Note (2026-11-26): OpenAI's Help Center article on healthcare model configurations says they are available to API organizations, and that a ChatGPT for Healthcare or ChatGPT Enterprise workspace is not required. The article says to pass a supported healthcare model ID, for example gpt-6.2-astra-healthcare, in a Responses API request, and that web search must be enabled to use the healthcare search index. The article says access does not by itself authorize protected health information, and that processing it requires an applicable Business Associate Agreement. The article does not name gpt-6.2-sol-healthcare, does not list a price, and does not print a calendar date. The API pricing page linked from that article lists Standard rates per 1M tokens of $8.00 input, $40.00 output, and $0.40 cached input for gpt-6.2-astra-healthcare, and $2.00 input, $10.00 output, and $0.10 cached input for gpt-6.2-sol-healthcare. That Standard table's 30m write and 12h write columns list $10.00 and $20.00 for gpt-6.2-astra-healthcare, and $2.50 and $5.00 for gpt-6.2-sol-healthcare. Fast rates on that page are $16.00 input, $80.00 output, and $0.80 cached input for gpt-6.2-astra-healthcare, and $4.00 input, $20.00 output, and $0.20 cached input for gpt-6.2-sol-healthcare. The page says promotional pricing for GPT-6.2 Astra Healthcare and GPT-6.2 Sol Healthcare, among other named models, is available at least through December 31, 2026. It does not say these Standard or Fast rates end on that date.$xw$
  ELSE description || $xw$ Note (2026-11-26): OpenAI's Help Center article on healthcare model configurations says they are available to API organizations, and that a ChatGPT for Healthcare or ChatGPT Enterprise workspace is not required. The article says to pass a supported healthcare model ID, for example gpt-6.2-astra-healthcare, in a Responses API request, and that web search must be enabled to use the healthcare search index. The article says access does not by itself authorize protected health information, and that processing it requires an applicable Business Associate Agreement. The article does not name gpt-6.2-sol-healthcare, does not list a price, and does not print a calendar date. The API pricing page linked from that article lists Standard rates per 1M tokens of $8.00 input, $40.00 output, and $0.40 cached input for gpt-6.2-astra-healthcare, and $2.00 input, $10.00 output, and $0.10 cached input for gpt-6.2-sol-healthcare. That Standard table's 30m write and 12h write columns list $10.00 and $20.00 for gpt-6.2-astra-healthcare, and $2.50 and $5.00 for gpt-6.2-sol-healthcare. Fast rates on that page are $16.00 input, $80.00 output, and $0.80 cached input for gpt-6.2-astra-healthcare, and $4.00 input, $20.00 output, and $0.20 cached input for gpt-6.2-sol-healthcare. The page says promotional pricing for GPT-6.2 Astra Healthcare and GPT-6.2 Sol Healthcare, among other named models, is available at least through December 31, 2026. It does not say these Standard or Fast rates end on that date.$xw$
END, "updatedAt" = now() WHERE slug = $xw$openai-api$xw$ AND COALESCE(description, $xw$$xw$) NOT LIKE $xw$%gpt-6.2-astra-healthcare%$xw$;

UPDATE platforms SET description = CASE
  WHEN COALESCE(description, $xw$$xw$) = $xw$$xw$ THEN $xw$Note (2026-11-26): Manus's help article on the Black Friday 2026 offer says the discount is time-limited and is not the regular price. It ends on 30 November 2026 at 23:59:59 Eastern Time (UTC-5). It applies to the first billing period only, the first month on monthly billing or the first year on annual billing. On the web, the Pro $100 tier is $90 for the first month or $900 for the first year, and the Max $200 tier is $160 for the first month or $1,600 for the first year. Pro tiers at $20, $40, $60, and $80 are not included. Max tiers above $200 get the same 20 percent off their regular price for that first period. Team plans are not included. In the iOS and Android apps the offer is listed for the Pro $100 and Max $200 tiers, and the store sets the price in local currency, so it can differ from these USD web examples. After the first period the subscription renews at the regular price shown at checkout. Prices earlier in this description are the earlier help-center list, not this offer.$xw$
  ELSE description || $xw$ Note (2026-11-26): Manus's help article on the Black Friday 2026 offer says the discount is time-limited and is not the regular price. It ends on 30 November 2026 at 23:59:59 Eastern Time (UTC-5). It applies to the first billing period only, the first month on monthly billing or the first year on annual billing. On the web, the Pro $100 tier is $90 for the first month or $900 for the first year, and the Max $200 tier is $160 for the first month or $1,600 for the first year. Pro tiers at $20, $40, $60, and $80 are not included. Max tiers above $200 get the same 20 percent off their regular price for that first period. Team plans are not included. In the iOS and Android apps the offer is listed for the Pro $100 and Max $200 tiers, and the store sets the price in local currency, so it can differ from these USD web examples. After the first period the subscription renews at the regular price shown at checkout. Prices earlier in this description are the earlier help-center list, not this offer.$xw$
END, "updatedAt" = now() WHERE slug = $xw$manus$xw$ AND COALESCE(description, $xw$$xw$) NOT LIKE $xw$%Black Friday 2026 offer says the discount is time-limited%$xw$;
